The author modifies a previously established method by Stieltjes to derive asymptotic formulas for the orthogonal polynomials $\PN$ that meet the condition:
\begin{equation}
\i_{-1}^{1} \NP(x)\log\frac{1}{1-x^2}\dx = 1
\end{equation}
for every $N\in\mathbb N$, using a novel approach. A novel comparison is made between this special case of the weight function and the Wigner semicircle distribution.
